WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.344
Hi, my name is David Lee, founder of CapExLayer.

00:00:03.344 --> 00:00:11.889
My goal is simple: remove the friction between where your revenue organization is today and the commercial result it needs to produce next.

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:22.291
That might mean creating qualified pipeline, moving a strategic account forward, shortening the path to a decision, increasing revenue, or protecting profit from the opportunities you already have.

00:00:22.291 --> 00:00:25.263
Most teams do not have an idea problem.

00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:27.121
They have a movement problem.

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:38.638
They may be targeting too many accounts, entering too late, missing the real decision-makers, allowing important deals to stall, or leaving good decisions trapped in meetings without clear ownership and follow-through.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:42.725
Another report or another general strategy session does not fix that.

00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:48.297
The work has to begin with the actual commercial constraint and end with visible movement.

00:00:48.297 --> 00:00:50.898
Start with the constraint that matters now.

00:00:50.898 --> 00:00:57.957
CapExLayer provides a focused path for account timing, enterprise opportunity movement, execution, founder capacity, or a coordinated ninety-day activation.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.558
The first path is Account Timing Activation.

00:01:00.558 --> 00:01:15.047
This is for an enterprise revenue team with a large market that needs to know which accounts deserve attention now, why the timing is credible, who matters inside the account, and what point of view will earn a conversation.

00:01:15.047 --> 00:01:23.963
The result is a prioritized commercial opening your team may not have found, supported by evidence, the right stakeholder, and a clear next action.

00:01:23.963 --> 00:01:26.935
The second path is the Enterprise Opportunity Workshop.

00:01:26.935 --> 00:01:32.508
This is for a team with one material opportunity valuable enough to deserve focused intervention.

00:01:32.508 --> 00:01:39.567
We map the champion, economic buyer, blockers, approval path, missing proof, and exact action required to advance the opportunity.

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:42.911
The result is not another discussion about the deal.

00:01:42.911 --> 00:01:48.483
It is a buyer path, a proof plan, an owner, and a dated advancement action.

00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:51.456
The third path is the Revenue Operating Sprint.

00:01:51.456 --> 00:01:57.028
This is for a team that already has strategy, but execution breaks down between meetings.

00:01:57.028 --> 00:02:04.087
We turn the commercial plan into owners, dates, reliable records, operating cadence, completed customer-facing work, and clear acceptance criteria.

00:02:04.087 --> 00:02:09.660
The result is a working revenue process your team can operate inside its current environment.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.632
The fourth path is the Founder Time-Back Partner.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:20.062
This is for a founder-led sales organization where the founder still carries too much preparation, coordination, follow-up, and commercial decision-making.

00:02:20.062 --> 00:02:23.406
The goal is not to remove the founder's judgment.

00:02:23.406 --> 00:02:30.837
It is to return the founder's time by moving revenue work forward without forcing every action to wait for them.

00:02:30.837 --> 00:02:36.409
The result is measured founder time returned and important commercial work advanced without sacrificing control.

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:39.381
The fifth path is the Ninety-Day Revenue Activation.

00:02:39.381 --> 00:02:46.440
This is for a team that needs better account selection, stronger opportunity strategy, and consistent operating execution working together.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:52.385
We focus the engagement around a defined commercial scorecard and run the system for ninety days.

00:02:52.385 --> 00:02:58.700
The result is visible movement across the accounts, opportunities, decisions, and execution milestones agreed at the start.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.044
Whichever path fits, the operating process remains the same.

00:03:02.044 --> 00:03:05.759
First, define the result, baseline, value, deadline, and decision owner.

00:03:05.759 --> 00:03:11.332
Second, diagnose the real constraint using market signals, customer evidence, pipeline truth, and process mapping.

00:03:11.332 --> 00:03:14.304
Third, activate the work required to create movement.

00:03:14.304 --> 00:03:19.505
Fourth, prove what changed and make a clear decision to expand, continue, or stop.

00:03:19.505 --> 00:03:25.821
If your team has a commercial result that must move in the next ninety days, start there.

00:03:25.821 --> 00:03:29.536
Bring the live account, opportunity, pipeline constraint, or executive bottleneck.

00:03:29.536 --> 00:03:36.595
We will identify the right starting point and define what meaningful progress should look like before the work begins.

00:03:36.595 --> 00:03:40.632
Book a qualified fifteen-minute conversation with me to discuss the outcome.
